{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":171,"line_start":135,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py"},"criterion":"A symbolic `--ref` is resolved ONCE at the close boundary and the resolved sha REPLACES the argument, so verification, snapshot materialisation, the drift guard and signing all see the same immutable commit (`_pin_completion_ref`, `transition_close.py:135`, rebound by the caller at `:618`).","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":411,"line_start":402,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py"},"criterion":"If the verified and signing shas ever disagree, the close emits a loud stderr warning naming BOTH shas and the exact remediation, and refuses to attest stale state (`transition_close.py:402-411`). OPERATOR DECISION 2026-08-28: a warning is SUFFICIENT.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":439,"line_start":418,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py"},"criterion":"A close that cannot obtain an attestation says so on stderr, naming the cause and how to certify. The machine-readable `completion_signature` marker is already present on the library, JSON and MCP surfaces. The residual — the default CLI text output on stdout not inspecting that marker — is tracked separately as `faulty-floppy-kob`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":152,"line_start":1,"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py"},"criterion":"A regression test drives a close with `--ref` advancing MID-RUN and asserts the close lands SIGNED and bound to the verified tree (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py`); seeding the defect back returns it to RED.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":618,"line_start":613,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py"},"criterion":"Bug 'Close gate races on a moving --ref: verification passes at one sha, signing refuses at another' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":615,"commits_inspected":2824,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":2266,"det_ms":5403.6,"diff_validation_ms":128,"distinct_references":2356,"git_history_read_ms":269,"landing_check_ms":1054,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":67424.7,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":5661,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":10,"structural_scan_ms":2247,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":36,"tool_calls":9,"total_ms":72881.1,"verifier_annotation_ms":0,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":1,"verifier_attempts_ms":251055,"verifier_between_attempts_ms":0,"verifier_build_drift_ms":375,"verifier_call_ms":251081,"verifier_code_snapshot_ms":127,"verifier_completion_agent_ms":67424,"verifier_dispatch_finalization_ms":0,"verifier_dispatch_ms":73481,"verifier_dispatch_setup_ms":600,"verifier_handle_apply_ms":0,"verifier_handle_defaults_ms":0,"verifier_handle_resolution_ms":173717,"verifier_inner_setup_ms":3855,"verifier_no_llm_passthrough_ms":0,"verifier_precheck_context_ms":5397,"verifier_resume_config_ms":0,"verifier_resume_count":0,"verifier_reusable_lookup_ms":25,"verifier_snapshot_enter_ms":0,"verifier_snapshot_exit_ms":0,"verifier_snapshot_gc_ms":1,"verifier_ticket_snapshot_ms":173213,"verifier_unclassified_workflow_steps_ms":0,"verifier_verdict_reconcile_ms":6,"verifier_workflow_ms":72881,"verifier_workflow_residual_ms":54,"verifier_workflow_step_count":7,"verifier_wrapper_finalization_ms":0,"verifier_wrapper_setup_ms":0,"verifier_wrapp